{
  "comment": "Agent SoW: the amendment review window (agentsow.com 0.26.0-draft, 5.8). A proposed replacement carries change_control.proposed_at inside its signed bytes. It lapses at proposed_at plus its review window, counted in days of 86,400 seconds. The window is the governing version's review_window_days (governing_window_days here; 7 where the governing version states none), or the proposal's own review_window_days where that is shorter; a longer value in the proposal does not lengthen its own window. The counterparty refuses a proposal whose proposed_at is later than the instant it received it. A new version forms when the proposer receives the approval before the lapse instant, or accepts one it receives later in its acknowledgement; the counterparty applies the new version only on that acknowledgement. Each case gives the instants and expects the lapse instant and the outcome: forms, lapsed, or refused. THE FIXTURE IS THE AUTHORITY: change it only with a spec change alongside.",
